# Force non-www (apex)
https://www.knoxvillesprayfoampros.com/* https://knoxvillesprayfoampros.com/:splat 301!

# Explicit /index.html -> / so the home has one canonical URL
/index.html / 301!

# Cloudflare Pages serves .html pages at their extensionless path with a 308 redirect from /*.html;
# we leave that implicit and rely on the host, so no `/*.html /:splat 308` rule here.

# Internal-only docs folder is never served. The `!` force flag makes this rule win
# over any file that happens to sit at /docs/... in the deploy output, so even if
# Cloudflare Pages uploads /docs/TRACKING.md it is not reachable from the web.
/docs/* /404.html 404!
# Legacy path (TRACKING.md used to live at the root; this stops any stale link).
/TRACKING.md /404.html 404!

# Catch-all: unknown URLs render /404.html with a real 404 status (NOT a soft 200, NOT a redirect to home)
/* /404.html 404
